\fs32 \cf4 \cb3 Hi everyone, I\'92m Rohan Nagpaul, a rising senior at Babson concentrating in Finance and entrepreneurship.\cb1 \
\cb3 I\'92d describe myself as someone who moves fast, thinks big, and is probably happiest when I\'92m building something that initially seems a little unreasonable.\cb1 \
\cb3 Most of my experience has been entrepreneurial. I started my first company as a teenager, later worked as the first employee at a YC-backed startup, and have spent the last few years building businesses of my own. Most recently, I co-founded Rauxmont Capital, an investment firm focused on private-market opportunities. We have grown to over $5 million in assets under management, and I spend most of my time sourcing investments, raising capital, working with founders, and figuring out how to get difficult deals across the finish line.\cb1 \
\cb3 At Babson, I\'92m also President of Sigma Phi Epsilon. That experience has taught me a completely different side of leadership. Managing a fraternity means dealing with a lot of personalities, motivating people who are not being paid to work for you, making decisions when not everyone agrees, and ultimately taking responsibility when something goes wrong. I\'92ve especially enjoyed rebuilding our alumni network, growing recruitment, and creating a stronger culture within the chapter.\cb1 \
\cb3 My biggest strength is probably resourcefulness. I\'92m comfortable being thrown into something I know very little about and figuring it out quickly. I\'92m also good at selling a vision, building relationships, negotiating, and getting people excited enough about an idea to actually do something about it.\'a0\cb1 \
\cb3 Outside of work, I\'92m into hockey, golf, traveling, great restaurants, and bringing interesting people together. I love meeting people who are obsessed with something and can teach me about a world I know nothing about. I dislike unnecessary bureaucracy, doing something a certain way just because that is how it has always been done, and meetings that probably could have been an email.\cb1 \
\cb3 My resume covers the more formal version of what I\'92ve done, but this is probably a better description of how I actually operate. I\'92m excited for the class; you can expect me to take ownership, move quickly, and care a lot about whatever we decide to build.\cb1 \
