\fs32 \cf4 \cb3 Hi all! I'm Ryan, a rising Senior at Babson concentrating in Sales and Entrepreneurship. I've been building and selling since I was 14, most recently as founder of RepliReach and as the sole rep working national healthcare conferences for Aventi Health. As I'm typing this, I'm working as an SDR intern for Samsara, getting daily practice when it comes to cold outreach and sales.\cb1 \
\uc0\u8232 \cb3 If you want to get me talking, two of my biggest passions are technology and electric scooters. If you've seen a blurry figure zipping around Babson's campus on an electric scooter, that was probably me. I also love debate - I'm on the E-board for Babson Debate Union and am always up for a good discussion.\cb1 \
\cb3 My strengths include closing and negotiating under pressure, rocket pitches and presenting, speed, and cross-cultural communication \'97 I've hired and worked with people from a lot of different countries. Mostly, I'm good at finding the unorthodox route when the front door is locked, and I take the blame when something is mine.\cb1 \
\cb3 In terms of weaknesses, my systems have historically been my ceiling. I generate results faster than I organize them, and building scalable structure is the specific reason I'm in this class. I'm also a doer well before I'm an idea person \'97 I'd rather execute a good idea hard than sit in ideation, so pair me with someone who loves the whiteboard.\cb1 \
\cb3 A bit of context on me: my parents are international teachers, so I grew up moving every few years \'97 they're relocating from Tokyo to Santiago this month. It got me used to amguity, change, and figuring things out on my own, which is probably why I default to trying to figure things out instead of doing nothing until crystal-clear instructions are given.\cb1 \
\cb3 The best evidence of how I work is Blue Oasis. I won a class-wide vote to lead 42 students on a marketing pop-up and was told the $200 budget was non-negotiable \'97 every group in the course's history had run on it. I spent the following week emailing companies anyway and came back with $2,000 in sponsorships from Crawford Software and Ken's Steak House, plus raffle funding, a DJ, carnival games, 300 free Red Bulls, and the Worcester Red Sox mascot. We had a record turnout of 250+, and Professor Gustafson now uses it as the course exemplar.\cb1 \
\cb3 I say all of this because with the way I work, if I'm given a constraint, there's a solid chance I'm going to not believe it and push higher. If you draft me, give me the hardest target on the board, because I love tackling problems that seem impossible.\cb1 \
