\fs32 \cf4 \cb3 Hi everyone!\cb1 \
\cb3 I'm Nandika Jain, a senior at Babson. I'm just getting back from a year at LSE in London - which meant a year of living and working alongside people from all over the world, each with a completely different way of seeing a problem. I loved it, and it's honestly a big part of why I'm excited for this class: some of the best thinking happens in a room full of people who don't exactly think like you.\cb1 \
\cb3 A little about me: I've always been the person who wants to understand what actually makes a company work - how it earns, what keeps people coming back, and where it's quietly fragile. That interest has pulled me across a lot of different rooms: finance, consulting, distressed assets, and a family business back home. Right now I'm helping build software for agriculture, which lets me sit at the intersection of technology, strategy, and storytelling all at once.\cb1 \
\cb3 What matters most to me in a team is the people. The best teams I've been part of ran on trust as much as talent - honest, accountable people who genuinely put everything into the work and actually enjoy doing it together. That's the kind of team I want to build.\cb1 \
\cb3 Outside of all that, I've travelled to more than 20 countries, I know the first 51 digits of pi by heart, and learning to fly a plane is somewhere near the top of my list. I've attached a profile with more on my background and how I work, but mostly I'm looking forward to meeting everyone and building something we're proud of this fall.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 Best regards,\'a0\cb1 \
\cb3 Nandika Jain.\'a0\cb1 \
