\cf4 \cb3 Hi everyone,\cb1 \
\cb3 My name is Adi Oberoi. Alongside my attached resume, wanted to share a bit more about who I am and how I work.\cb1 \
\cb3 I'm a rising senior, finishing up my degree in Business Analytics at Babson. I grew up around my family's advertising agency in Mumbai, so pitching, negotiating with clients, and adjusting when a campaign doesn't land the way you planned are all familiar territory for me. That background is a big part of why I chose this class. I wanted a structured, competitive environment to sharpen those instincts even further.\cb1 \
\cb3 People who know me well would say I walk into a room and start reading it almost immediately, figuring out who the real decision maker is and where the actual opportunity sits before most people have settled in. I stay calm under pressure and tend to move toward fixing a problem before others have finished reacting to it. My weak spot is more on the coordination side. In a past group project I assumed my grasp of the material would carry the final output, and I didn't communicate direction clearly enough, so everyone worked in isolation and the deliverable suffered for it. Since then I put more effort into aligning the team upfront so there's less cleanup at the end.\cb1 \
\cb3 Outside of class I play for Babson Squash Club, I've been doing commercial and voiceover work since I was five, and I just finished reading Shoe Dog by Phil Knight, which I'd recommend to anyone in this group. I like fast paced, high stakes environments where you have to think on your feet, and I don't love sitting on a decision longer than it needs to sit.\cb1 \
